+## Deferred from: code review of 9-3-implement-constraint-configuration-with-staged-validation-and-single-increment-config-version (2026-05-11)
+
+- **`_build_audit_changes(None, new)` does not read prior values from `config_audit_log` when `active_constraints` was manually purged** [`src/open_ems/storage/repositories/config_repo.py:121-144`] — Operator-recovery scenario: DBA DELETEs `active_constraints` rows but keeps audit history. The next activation produces an audit row with `previous_value={"kw": None}` even though the actual predecessor exists in `config_audit_log`. Cross-table `next_version` correctly preserves monotonicity but `previous_value` derivation is asymmetric. Reading audit-log for derived `previous_value` adds complexity and isn't part of 9.3's surface; address in a future storage-layer story that owns operator-purge recovery.
+- **Successful re-validation PASS is consumed in-memory and not persisted before the draft is DELETEd** [`src/open_ems/services/constraints.py` `activate_draft` step 5 + step 10] — The FAIL path calls `record_validation_outcome_locked` and persists the report; the PASS path skips persistence and proceeds to delete the draft at step 10. Audit/observability tools cannot retrieve the validation report that gated the activation. Depends on Story 9.4's deployment-validation read path — confirm whether 9.4 needs the persisted PASS report or only the `config_audit_log` rows (which carry the changed fields but not the full check breakdown).
+- **`record_validation_outcome_locked` exception on the FAIL persistence path masks the underlying validation FAIL** [`src/open_ems/services/constraints.py:240-248`] — If the in-lock UPDATE fails (transient DB error), the user sees a 500 instead of the contractual `constraints_validation_failed` 400 with the report payload. Rare path; harden when storage-error mapping gets a centralized sweep.
+- **"Validate" button does not auto-save the current form values before validating** [`src/open_ems/web/templates/installer/_setup_constraints_form.html:91-97`] — Two-click flow: user must click "Save draft" then "Validate". Clicking "Validate" without first saving returns `draft_not_found_for_session`. Spec is silent on this; the current behavior is contractual. Revisit during a UX-polish iteration if installer feedback identifies this as friction.
+
 ## Deferred from: code review of 9-1-implement-device-discovery-step-with-live-probing-capability-classification-and-manual-entry (2026-05-11)
 
 - **No delete-pending-entry route** [`src/open_ems/web/routes/setup.py` + `device_repo.py`] — Manual-entry probe crash before `mark_validated` leaves an orphan `validated=0` row. The installer can only `acknowledge-unvalidated` it (one-way) or wait for `mark_validated` from a subsequent successful retry — no delete path. Spec doesn't contract a delete endpoint; revisit when Epic 11 considers installer-side device-registry management.
